From dc61094b3e983e5f9ef73e607c6e09d035cdadfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:58:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homar search gesture: app search with the keyboard at once

Upstream's "Open app search" gesture slides up the A-Z drawer and only
then focuses the search field, so the icon grid shows first; and an
empty query (Lawnchair's zero state) answers with the A-Z list anyway.

New gesture option "Search (instant)", serial name homarSearch
(swipe_down_gesture_handler = {"type":"homarSearch"}), logic in
app/lawnchair/omalawn/HomarSearchGesture.kt:
- puts the drawer into search mode while off-screen (an empty result
  list; upstream's search transition takes 0 ms), shows ALL_APPS
  without the slide and focuses the field, raising the keyboard;
- while the query is empty the drawer keeps its empty search page
  (hook in AllAppsSearchInput.clearSearchResult);
- Back goes home, also with a query typed (upstream clears the query
  and drops to the A-Z list).

Hooks: the config object in GestureHandlerConfig (search icon), the
option in GestureHandlerOption and in the gesture option list of
GestureHandlerOptions.kt (left out with the deck layout, like upstream's
drawer gestures), and a three-line
GestureHandler subclass next to OpenAppSearchGestureHandler (the base
class is sealed to that package). The label is in
res/values/homar_strings.xml.

On Lawnchair 16 the search field loses focus when the keyboard goes
down, so the next Back reaches LawnchairLauncher.onStateBack, which
resets the search; with our empty search page kept, every Back would do
that again and the drawer stayed open. A one-line hook there sends Back
from our session home (HomarSearchGesture.onStateBack).
